        "description": "Iran's President Masoud Pezeshkian has apologised to neighbouring states and says Tehran will not attack them \"unless attacked first\", in a video address broadcast on state media.\n\nShortly after Pezeshkian's address aired, Qatar said it had intercepted a missile attack.\n\nThere's been an explosion near Dubai International Airport and the BBC has verified video that shows the apparent drone attack.\n\nSome flights are now taking off and landing at the airport, after authorities had earlier suspended operations.\n\nSubscribe here: http://bit.ly/1rbfUog\n\nFor more news, analysis and features visit: www.bbc.com/news \n\n#Iran #Gulf #MiddleEast #Dubai #BBCNews",
